# A chain through in gets a general help.
mode: syntax
---- query
from t | where a in (1) == true
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..32
  PIPELINE@0..31
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "t"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    PIPE@7..8 "|"
    WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
    WHERE_OP@9..31
      IDENT@9..14 "where"
      WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
      BIN_EXPR@15..31
        IN_EXPR@15..23
          NAME_REF@15..16
            IDENT@15..16 "a"
          WHITESPACE@16..17 " "
          IDENT@17..19 "in"
          WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
          ARG_LIST@20..23
            L_PAREN@20..21 "("
            LITERAL@21..22
              LONG@21..22 "1"
            R_PAREN@22..23 ")"
        WHITESPACE@23..24 " "
        EQ2@24..26 "=="
        WHITESPACE@26..27 " "
        LITERAL@27..31
          TRUE_KW@27..31 "true"
  WHITESPACE@31..32 "\n"

error[DS0101]: comparison operators cannot be chained
  --> query:1:25
  |
1 | from t | where a in (1) == true
  |                -------- ^^ a second comparison
  |                |
  |                the result of this comparison is not a value to compare again
  |
  = help: compare each pair separately and combine them with `and`
